                <pb facs="0503" n="495" xml:id="pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.51/362: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-03T19:00:00-04:00">October 3, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>161. Foreign Minister states Soler has been instructed accept economic
                    cooperation program as outlined in Department’s telegram no. 62, July 23, 4 p.m.
                    He also expressed the hope that additional [$] 100,000 can be secured for
                    mandioca development. I again urge this.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
